      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs31 #24): a read-only system
      ⍝ variable (e.g. ⎕TS) in a NON-FINAL vector-assignment position
      ⍝ used to pass Symbol::can_be_assigned() (NC_left alone doesn't
      ⍝ exclude it) and reach Symbol::vector_assignment(), whose
      ⍝ assign() is a silent no-op for a read-only variable -- so ⎕TS
      ⍝ was silently dropped while the other names in the same vector
      ⍝ assignment still got assigned. Must be consistent with plain
      ⍝ ⎕TS←7 (SYNTAX ERROR) instead, with NO partial assignment to any
      ⍝ of the other names either, regardless of ⎕TS's position.
      ⍝
      A←0 ⋄ B←0
      (⎕TS A B)←7 8 9
SYNTAX ERROR+
      (⎕TS A B)←7 8 9
             ^  ^
      )MORE
Assignment to read-only system variable ⎕TS
      )SIC
      A B
0 0

      (⎕TS A)←7 8
SYNTAX ERROR+
      (⎕TS A)←7 8
           ^  ^
      )SIC
      A
0

      (A ⎕TS B)←7 8 9
SYNTAX ERROR+
      (A ⎕TS B)←7 8 9
             ^  ^
      )SIC
      A B
0 0

      ⍝ control: ⎕TS as the FINAL (rightmost) name already correctly
      ⍝ SYNTAX ERRORed before this fix too (a different code path --
      ⍝ Symbol::resolve_left() -- handles the last name)
      ⍝
      (A ⎕TS)←7 8
SYNTAX ERROR+
      (A ⎕TS)←7 8
            ^ ^
      )SIC
      A
0

      ⍝ control: an all-ordinary vector assignment is unaffected
      ⍝
      A←0 ⋄ B←0 ⋄ C←0
      (A B C)←7 8 9
      A B C
7 8 9

      )ERASE A B C

      ⍝ IBM APL2 compatibility ----------------------------------

      ∇Z←SHOW_NC B¯B;N
       N←8↑B,':'
       →(¯1 0 1 2 3 4 = ⎕NC B¯B)/I U L V F O ◊ ++
      I: →0, Z←(8↑B), ': Invalid Name'
      U: →0, Z←(8↑B), ': Unused Name'
      L: →0, Z←(8↑B), ': Label'
      V: →0, Z←(8↑B), ': Value', ⍎B¯B
      F: →0, Z←(8↑B), ': Function'
      O: →0, Z←(8↑B), ': Operator'
      ∇

      ∇Z←A (LO OPER1) B
       SHOW_NC 'A'
       SHOW_NC 'LO'
       SHOW_NC 'OPER1'
       SHOW_NC 'B'
      ∇

      ∇Z←A (LO OPER2 RO) B
       SHOW_NC 'A'
       SHOW_NC 'LO'
       SHOW_NC 'OPER1'
       SHOW_NC 'RO'
       SHOW_NC 'B'
      ∇

      ⊣««« ⍝ NOTE: IBM APL2 gives:

      ⍝ binding of bracket index
      ⍝
      1 2 3[2]
      RANK ERROR

      ⍝ binding of left operand (literal)
      ⍝
      11 22 33 OPER1 1 2 3
      A       : Unused Name
      LO      : Value  11 22 33
      OPER1   : Operator
      B       : Value  1 2 3

      ⍝ binding of left operand (parser)
      ⍝
      (UU VV WW)←11 22 33
      A       : Unused Name
      LO      : Value  11 22 33
      OPER1   : Operator
      B       : Value  1 2 3

      ⍝ binding of left operand (in parentheses)
      ⍝
      11 22 (33 OPER1) 1 2 3
      A       : 11
      LO      : Value  22 33
      OPER1   : Operator
      B       : Value  1 2 3

      ⍝ binding of left and right operands (literal)
      ⍝
      11 22 33 'lop' OPER2 'rop' 1 2 3
      A:      Value Unused Name
      LO:     Value lop
      OPER1:  Operator
      RO:     Value rop
      B:      Value 1 2 3
       »»»


